WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
Tesla Shorts Time Daily Episode 429.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.740
Hey, it's Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.080
Thanks for joining me on Tesla Shorts Time Daily.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.480
Today is April 7th, 2026.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.940
Let's catch up on what actually moved the needle

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.140
for Tesla in the last 24 hours.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.100
The biggest headline is that Tesla has once again

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.160
taken the global EV sales crown in the first quarter,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.520
edging out BYD.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.840
Even though the company's own vehicle deliveries

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.460
only grew about 6% year over year.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.100
That's a modest increase by Tesla's historical standards,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.260
and it came during a period when EV growth slowed

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.760
in several key regions.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.040
At the same time, the energy business

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.180
posted a roughly 15% decline,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.320
which probably raised a few eyebrows

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.740
heading into earning season.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.860
According to EVTech.News,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.100
the results still underline Tesla's

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.200
scale advantage and the strength of its brand.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.620
Even when the broader market gets choppy,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.280
buyers keep choosing Tesla when they decide

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.360
to go pure electric.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.500
I think what's interesting here

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.040
is how the narrative has shifted.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.900
A few years ago, 6% growth would have felt like a disappointment.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.140
Now, against a backdrop of softening demand in Europe

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.100
and parts of China,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.940
holding the top spot feels like a quiet flex.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.600
It suggests that Tesla's combination of software features,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.600
brand Keshe, and consistent product improvements

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.240
still give it an edge that pure hardware competitors

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.680
are finding hard to replicate.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.080
For the business itself, this matters

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.020
because it shows the company can defend

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.240
its position without needing explosive growth

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.200
everywhere at once.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.300
It also gives management a bit more breathing room

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.980
as they juggle everything from new vehicle programs

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.440
to autonomy development.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.340
The wind isn't flashy,

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.380
but it's the kind of steady positioning

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:40.740
that compounds over time.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.440
That global picture looks even more nuanced

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.620
when you zoom into specific markets.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.680
In South Korea, Tesla posted a staggering

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.160
335% jump in first quarter deliveries.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.920
That number stands in sharp contrast

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.420
to the overall 6% growth globally

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.060
and the softness we're seeing in some other regions.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.460
According to tip ranks, the surge highlights

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.780
how demand can stay remarkably resilient

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:05.680
in certain countries

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.400
when the right conditions line up.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.940
Local incentives improved model-y availability

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.220
and growing familiarity with the brand

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.880
all seem to be playing a role.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.220
What I find encouraging is that

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.740
it shows Tesla isn't uniformly exposed

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.180
to the same headwinds.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.700
While some markets are clearly cooling,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.420
others are still accelerating.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.480
That kind of geographic diversification is healthy.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.900
It reminds me that the EV slowdown story

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.680
we keep hearing isn't a straight line.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:33.860
It's patchy.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.940
Product mix matters too.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.440
In South Korea, the mix of available models

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.260
and perhaps some refreshed versions

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.880
seem to be landing exactly where buyers are.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.280
For Tesla's longer-term strategy,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.540
this kind of result validates the decision

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.580
to keep refining the existing lineup

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.320
while the next generation of vehicles

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.540
is still in development.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.480
It's proof that the current cars

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.920
still have plenty of runway in the right markets.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.520
Good sales momentum is always nicer

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.880
when it's paired with fewer headaches in Washington.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.740
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.900
has officially closed its investigation

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.160
into Tesla's remote control feature.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.720
The probe started in early 2025

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.020
after about 100 reported crashes

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.660
involving nearly 2.6 million vehicles.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.860
According to Inside EVs,

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.080
the closure removes one lingering cloud

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.000
that had been hanging over the advanced

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.800
driver assistance side of the business.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.400
For a company that moves as fast

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.040
on software as Tesla does,

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.020
every open regulatory file creates uncertainty

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.740
that can slow down releases

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.500
and distract engineering teams.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.480
What's striking is how little detail has come out

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.960
about exactly why the investigation closed.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.840
That lack of fanfare makes me think

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.380
the issue may have been narrower

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.260
than the initial headline suggested.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.340
Either way, it's a quiet but meaningful win.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.500
Tesla can now push forward with software updates

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.900
and future autonomy work

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.660
without that particular overhang.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.240
Of course, safety questions around new features

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.080
will keep coming.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.640
That's the territory Tesla operates in.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.880
The closure feels like validation

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.360
that the data Tesla provided

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:06.720
satisfied the agency,

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.100
which should give owners a bit more confidence

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.000
and give the company a cleaner runway

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.480
heading into the rest of the year.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.420
With one less thing to worry about from regulators,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.560
Tesla is turning its attention back to the

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.080
everyday infrastructure that owners actually touch.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.360
The company just opened a new charging hub

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.120
in Navi Mumbai,

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.180
right in the Mumbai metropolitan area.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.900
According to Indika News,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.080
the site strengthens the supercharger footprint in India

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.460
and gives current owners a more reliable network

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.860
while the company figures out

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.840
its longer-term plans for the country.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.720
Reliable charging is still one of the tallest barriers

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.400
to EV adoption in emerging markets like India.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:42.700
Range is one thing,

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.560
but the fear of being stranded somewhere

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.060
without a fast charger is something else entirely.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.760
By putting steel in the ground

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.440
before launching vehicles at scale,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.700
Tesla is following its classic playbook.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.280
Build the network first,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.200
then bring the cars.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.360
The timing feels strategic too.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.240
India is slowly warming to electric mobility.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.440
Policy support is improving in some states

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.500
and Tesla has been weighing its entry options carefully.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.520
This new hub won't single-handedly change the market,

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.440
but it improves the ownership experience

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.660
for the early adopters

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.540
who are already driving Tesla's there.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.440
It also sends a clear signal

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.360
that the company is serious about India

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.140
rather than just testing the waters.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.640
That infrastructure-heavy mindset

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.260
stands in pretty stark contrast

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.860
to how Tesla's biggest rival

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.580
is approaching the same challenge.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.480
BYD and Tesla are clearly pursuing different philosophies

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.900
when it comes to supporting their electric vehicles.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.700
Tesla keeps doubling down

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.180
on its supercharger network,

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.700
treating fast charging as a core part of the ownership promise.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.780
BYD, on the other hand,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.680
has leaned into alternative pathways

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.140
that include more partnerships,

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:46.760
home-charging emphasis,

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.560
and in some cases battery-swapping concepts

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.600
in certain markets.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.700
According to CleanTechnica,

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.580
this contrast reveals how infrastructure philosophy

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.320
ends up shaping brand positioning

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.260
and the day-to-day customer experience

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.360
in ways that go beyond the cars themselves.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.180
I find this difference genuinely fascinating

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.860
because there isn't one universally correct answer.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.540
In North America and Europe,

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.320
Tesla's closed ecosystem of superchargers

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.840
has built enormous trust.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.260
Owners know they can travel long distances with confidence.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.760
In other parts of the world,

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.060
different economics and different consumer habits

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.600
might reward BYD's more flexible approach.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.940
For the broader industry, this split is healthy.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.140
It forces everyone to keep innovating

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.360
on both the vehicle side and the energy side.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.580
As the transition accelerates,

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.240
we'll get to see which model scales more efficiently

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.720
and which one customers ultimately prefer

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:37.600
in different regions.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.800
My sense is both strategies

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.440
will coexist for a long time

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.820
and the winners will be the ones

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.320
that adapt fastest to local conditions.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.080
That competitive pressure

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.340
is showing up in product announcements as well.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.500
Rivian just teased details on its upcoming R2 compact SUV,

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:57.880
claiming it could deliver 335 miles of EPA range

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.760
at a price below $60,000.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.320
That's a combination Tesla has not yet matched

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:04.860
in that segment of the market.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.220
According to how to geek,

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.820
the claim puts noticeable pressure

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.500
on whatever Tesla eventually brings

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.180
to the compact crossover space.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.900
For customers, it's exciting

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.660
because it suggests range anxiety

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.280
at more accessible price points

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.240
might ease faster than many expected

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.560
across the whole industry.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.760
What stands out to me is how quickly

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.280
the goalposts keep moving.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:24.840
Not that long ago,

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.040
300 miles of range

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.680
at that price would have seemed ambitious.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.180
Now it's becoming the new benchmark competitors

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:30.760
are setting.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.940
It's a reminder that battery chemistry,

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.120
thermal management and vehicle efficiency

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.780
are all improving steadily,

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.220
and no single company has a permanent lead.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.320
Tesla will obviously have its own

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.700
next-generation compact models in development,

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.600
but the timeline and final specs are still under wraps.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:47.980
In the meantime,

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.260
announcements like Rivians keep the entire sector honest.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.780
They force everyone to keep pushing on cost

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.720
and performance rather than coasting on past advantages.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.180
We'll see how Tesla chooses to respond

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.960
when those vehicles finally arrive,

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.760
but the bar is clearly rising.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.740
While the product race heats up,

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.120
one of Tesla's most visible institutional

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.860
supporters just doubled down.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.700
Kathy Woods' arc funds

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.880
bought roughly $14 million worth of Tesla shares

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.200
across three different exchange-traded funds

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.780
during the recent price pullback.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.500
According to Benzinga,

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.440
the purchases reflect continued long-term conviction

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.780
from one of the company's most outspoken believers.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.580
This comes at a moment

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.920
when several more traditional Wall Street voices

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.620
have grown noticeably more cautious

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.920
about valuation and near-term growth.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:34.800
I've always viewed Kathy's approach

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.960
as a high-conviction bet

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:38.240
on the full stack of Tesla's technology

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.800
from energy to autonomy to robotics.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.400
Buying on weakness is classic for her,

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.080
and it often generates chatter

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.320
about whether smart money sees current levels

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.440
as attractive again.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.120
Of course, one fund's buying

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.920
doesn't change the underlying fundamentals,

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.040
but it does tend to influence sentiment.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.600
In a market that can swing dramatically

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.140
on quarterly delivery numbers

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.620
or a single-riviant announcement,

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.460
these kinds of moves get noticed.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.380
It will be interesting to see

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.840
whether this latest vote of confidence proves well-timed

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.460
or whether broader economic conditions

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.320
end up testing that conviction further.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:10.360
It's also worth sitting

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.320
with the regulatory story for an extra minute

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.060
because it carries some important context.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.840
The NHTSA closing its remote control investigation

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.160
is clearly positive.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.340
Yet it follows months of scrutiny

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:23.680
and reports of about 100 crashes

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:27.200
involving a fleet of nearly 2.6 million vehicles.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.780
Those numbers are tiny

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:32.180
when you consider how many miles Tesla vehicles drive every day,

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.960
but headlines around any crash involving advanced driver assistance

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.080
tend to land hard.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:39.640
The episode is a useful reminder

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.020
of how quickly safety questions can escalate

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.980
even when the statistical record looks relatively clean.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.180
The good news is that Tesla now has one less distraction

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.100
and can iterate faster on software.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.260
At the same time,

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.780
the company will need to keep showing

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.260
that its validation process

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.080
is stay ahead of what regulators

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.260
and the public expect.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.840
I think this tension between innovation speed

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.280
and thorough safety proofing

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.620
is going to remain a central theme for years.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.880
Tesla has demonstrated it can adapt after incidents,

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.020
but the scrutiny isn't going away.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.560
Getting the balance right

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:11.980
is one of the hardest parts

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.020
of trying to bring autonomous technology

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:15.220
into the world at scale.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.600
The closure feels like a step forward,

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.240
but it doesn't close the book

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.580
on the broader conversation.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.900
Taking a step back from the daily noise,

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:24.780
it's worth applying some first principles

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.600
thinking to something that could matter a lot in the years ahead.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.820
When do battery electric heavy trucks

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.940
actually become economically superior

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.980
to diesel for most real-world duty cycles?

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:35.640
The answer, surprisingly,

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.060
isn't mainly about the absolute cost

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:39.800
per kilowatt hour of batteries.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.340
It's far more sensitive to annual mileage,

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.420
electricity rates,

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.240
and how well the charging infrastructure

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.580
matches real freight routes.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:47.880
Think about it.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:50.320
A typical North American class eight truck

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:54.780
might travel between 120,000 and 150,000 kilometers a year.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:59.160
At electricity prices of 12 to 15 cents per kilowatt hour,

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.740
and today's diesel prices,

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.820
the fuel savings alone can offset

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:06.980
a 150,000 to $200,000 higher upfront cost

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.900
within about three years for high utilization fleets,

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:13.680
assuming efficiency around two to three kilowatt hours per kilometer.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:17.180
But if utilization drops or charging access is poor,

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:18.720
the math flips quickly.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.980
Lower mileage routes or remote operations

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.080
still favor diesel.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.200
This is why Tesla designs the semi the way it does.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:27.540
From the ground up,

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.340
it uses cell-to-pack integration

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:32.140
and structural battery elements to cut weight and cost.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.780
At the same time, the company is deliberately placing

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:36.820
mega-chargers at high traffic depots

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.220
so fleets can actually hit the utilization numbers

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.140
the physics demands.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.080
Tesla treats energy cost and uptime

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.400
as first-order variables

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.720
rather than simply dropping big batteries

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.600
into an existing diesel chassis.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:52.280
The bet is that it can reshape enough of the freight network

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.160
through better route predictability,

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.320
depot charging, and fleet optimization

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.260
to make those favorable conditions the norm

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.720
rather than the exception.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.160
Infragmented, low mileage or remote operations,

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.500
diesel will probably keep the edge for a while.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.440
The real question is how quickly Tesla

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.640
and the industry can tilt the playing field.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.360
Before we wrap up, keep an eye tomorrow

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:17.380
on how the market digests these mixed delivery signals

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.540
alongside the latest competitive claims

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.760
coming from both Rivian and BYD.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:23.500
The story is never simple,

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.140
but that's what makes it interesting.

